# musician: the page turn. The beat scheduler runs this when the context
# reaches its rotate horizon (`kj transport rotate --every N`), after it has
# detached the context from its track in the same beat.
#
# `kj context rotate` replaces this context with a successor that runs the
# `create` lifecycle again: fresh stance, chair, primer and loadout, the same
# label, and a copy of the beat attachment, which `create/S20-arm.kai`
# announces to the track. The predecessor is archived. The track's clock does
# not pause. See docs/chameleon.md, "Players".
set -e
kj context rotate
